From d6fe9c1b02ad4ea562db2803869630b1aec04f7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 14:45:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Hades][GBM] HadesFramePackingCheck: does the driver take
 frame packing

For the card "3D: frame packing" of Check this setup: the builtin asks
the driver, with the display connected and no 3D video, whether it
takes the HDMI 3D frame-packed mode that the display declares (1080p
at 24000/1001 first, as the driver lists it), in test commits only:
nothing changes on the screen. The buffers asked are those a 3D video
would go out in: one of the kind of the window's of that mode (8 bits;
on nvidia-drm linear and as wide as the second eye needs), as GBM makes
it, and on nvidia-drm Kodi's own dumb buffers, made and checked as for
a video, so that whether the GPU draws into them or the processor
copies is known too (FramePackingCheck.h).

The answer, a line of JSON, goes to the property hades.check.fp.result
of the Home window and to kodi.log: taken, refused (with what the
driver answered), no frame-packed mode, or not asked. The test commit
of a frame-packed mode is shared with the one of FramePackedOwnStart()
(AskFramePacked()), which keeps what it asked.
